            "solve-equation-negative-coefficient"
          ],
          "archetype": "lr-audit:parameter-extension+lr-audit:rearrange-extension",
          "rationale": "Classification of revised source content; no teaching-content edits.",
          "sourcePages": [
            93
          ],
          "sourceTargetId": "page-93-q6-c"
        },
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k = 12$",
          "worked": "Rearranging $kx - 3y = k$ gives $3y = kx - k \\implies y = \\frac{k}{3}x - \\frac{k}{3}$. The second equation has gradient $4$. For no solution, the lines must be parallel: $\\frac{k}{3} = 4 \\implies k = 12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
